<description>
Move each gray bar into its adjacent orange rectangle as full stripes from the contacted edge.

Input structure
- The scene uses black outside space, yellow fill, gray one-cell-thick bars, and solid orange rectangles.
- Each gray bar 4-touches exactly one orange rectangle; some orange rectangles have no touching gray bar.
- Gray bars touching the same orange rectangle all have the same orientation.

Rule
- Recolor every original gray cell to yellow.
- For each orange rectangle touched by gray bars, count the gray cells assigned to that rectangle.
- Horizontal gray bars repaint that many cells as complete orange rows starting from the contacted top or bottom row.
- Vertical gray bars repaint that many cells as complete orange columns starting from the contacted left or right column.
- Orange rectangles with no touching gray bar remain unchanged.

Key insight
- The gray pixels are not copied by shape; their count is transferred into the neighboring orange rectangle as edge-aligned row or column stripes.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "gray one-cell-thick bars s",
  "dst": "4-adjacent solid orange rectangles d",
  "match_cond": "s 4-touches d",
  "transform": "erase s to yellow; in each matched d, repaint |matched s cells| orange cells gray as complete rows for horizontal bars or complete columns for vertical bars from the touched edge"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10-18 rows x 14-18 cols
  background: black (0) border surrounding a solid yellow (4) content rectangle
  border_thickness: 0-4 cells per side (at least one side may be 0)
  content_region: 6-13 rows x 12-15 cols, filled with yellow except for orange rects and gray bars
  orange_rects:
    count: 1-4 per grid
    shape: solid rectangle, 1-5 rows x 2-6 cols, area 4-12
    placement: each touches exactly one edge of the content region (top/bottom/left/right)
    untouched: 0-1 orange rects have no adjacent gray bars and remain unchanged in output
  gray_bars:
    count: 2-6 per grid, 1-2 bars per orange rect
    shape: one-cell-thick (h=1 or w=1), length 1-7
    placement: on the same content-edge row/col as their paired orange rect, extending outward with zero column/row overlap with the orange
    orientation: bars on top/bottom edge are horizontal (h=1); bars on left/right edge are vertical (w=1); singletons resolved by contact direction
    contact: each bar 4-touches exactly one orange rect at its extreme row (top or bottom) or column (left or right)
    all bars for one orange touch the same extreme edge of that orange
  divisibility_constraint: total gray area for each orange rect divides evenly by orange width (horizontal) or height (vertical); stripe_count 1 to full fill
  transform: erase gray to yellow; repaint stripe_count complete rows/cols of orange to gray from the contacted edge inward

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size and content region with black border.
    2. Place 1-4 orange rects flush against distinct edges of the content region (no overlap between rects or their edge neighborhoods).
    3. For each orange rect that will have bars (all but 0-1), pick orientation matching its edge (H for top/bottom, V for left/right).
    4. Choose stripe_count (1 to full dimension). Compute total_gray = stripe_count * orange_width_or_height.
    5. Split total_gray into 1-2 bar lengths. Each bar is placed on the same content-edge row/col, adjacent to the orange but not overlapping its span. Ensure bars fit within the content region and don't collide with other components.
    6. In the output, fill stripe_count rows/cols of the orange from the contacted edge with gray. The input has the gray bars placed as computed and the orange fully orange.
```
</generation_spec>
